                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
            and such that the homomorphism above then
            %em induces
            the previous 1-equivariant data by transgression.
          %p
            Such a “localization” of equivariant elliptic cohomology seems to be just what is being vaguely hinted at in (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, section 5.1
            ) under the name “
            %a{:href => "#2EquivariantEllipticCohomology"}> 2-equivariant elliptic cohomology
            ”, we discuss this in more detail
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#2EquivariantEllipticCohomology"} below
          %p
            Hence we arrive at a refinement of the above
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong slogan
          %ul
